053 \\quad\\land\\quad 127401 < 529053","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>127401</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>529053</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>127401</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>529053</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>127401</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>529053</mn></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"the_same_arithmetic_answers_more_than_one_domain","name":"CLAIMED: 1644 formula-shaped statements carry 1572 distinct byte-strings and 1439 distinct algebraic forms, so 205 statements restate a form another already holds — and those split 129 copies against 15 crosses, the widest cross spanning 3 wings. Most repetition is waste; a small part of it is a bridge.","statement":"((1439 < 1572) ∧ (1644 - 1439 = 205)) ∧ ((129 > 8 * 15) ∧ (3 > 2))","address":"6eebc85c-d501-8b58-ab00-fbae9c1f40c0","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"1439 < 1572 \\quad\\land\\quad 1644 - 1439 = 205 \\quad\\land\\quad 129 > 8 \\cdot 15 \\quad\\land\\quad 3 > 2","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1439</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1572</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>1644</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1439</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>205</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>129</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"the_generated_closure_partitions_into_three_kinds","name":"CLAIMED: of 2383726 crosses the corpus's own integers generate, 1854179 are forced by an operator's algebra, 494 are stated, and 529053 remain — and the three account for the whole, 1854179 + 494 + 529053 = 2383726, with the forced between 3 and 4 times the unstated.","statement":"(1854179 + 494 + 529053 = 2383726) ∧ ((1854179 > 3 * 529053) ∧ (1854179 < 4 * 529053))","address":"e1883d2b-60e3-8d5a-95f3-10a0a41853a2","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"1854179 + 494 + 529053 = 2383726 \\quad\\land\\quad 1854179 > 3 \\cdot 529053 \\quad\\land\\quad 1854179 < 4 \\cdot 529053","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1854179</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>494</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>529053</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2383726</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>1854179</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>529053</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>1854179</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>529053</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null},{"key":"the_corpus_has_sealed_under_a_hundredth_of_its_own_closure","name":"CLAIMED: the 1644 formula-shaped statements across 113 wings are built from 1411 distinct integers and state 494 crosses, against 529053 their own integers generate unstated — fewer than one in a hundred, since 494 × 100 < 529053, at between 14 and 15 formulas per wing.","statement":"((494 * 100 < 529053) ∧ (1411 > 113)) ∧ ((113 * 14 ≤ 1644) ∧ (113 * 15 > 1644))","address":"34e3faa7-53d9-87f7-975d-1a6d2ef6bbb2","skill":"cross-formulas","tex":"494 \\cdot 100 < 529053 \\quad\\land\\quad 1411 > 113 \\quad\\land\\quad 113 \\cdot 14 \\le 1644 \\quad\\land\\quad 113 \\cdot 15 > 1644","mathml":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>494</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>529053</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mn>1411</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>113</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>113</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1644</mn></mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo>∧</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mrow><mrow><mn>113</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1644</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></math>","exercise":null}],"exercises":0}
